  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Installation of internally illuminated hanging projecting sign and internally illuminated fascia sign at first floor level",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed signage, by reason of its internal illumination and use of acrylic materials,&amp;nbsp;leads to less than substantial harm to the significance of a designated heritage asset, the&amp;nbsp;Grade II listed building at 143 Lower Clapton Road, without securing a public benefit, and fails to&amp;nbsp;conserve or enhance and reveal the significance of the non-designated asset, the locally listed building at 135 Lower Clapton Road and its setting. The proposal is therefore contrary to policies PP1 (Public Realm),&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), LP4 (Non-Designated Heritage Assets), and LP7 (Advertisements) of Hackney&#x27;s Local Plan LP33 (2020), and policies D4 (Delivering good design), D8 (Public realm), and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of The London Plan. (2021)&amp;nbsp; and Hackney&#x27;s Commercial Extension and Alterations SPD (2026).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
